notes.ai — running assistant notes (user-managed)
====================================================


2026-01-20
- Added boot intro animation: rapid falling tetrominoes that fill the 16x16 matrix (skippable via any input).
  Config: INTRO_ENABLED / INTRO_MAX_MS / INTRO_FRAME_MS / INTRO_MAX_FRAMES_PER_PIECE.
- Implemented Serial-open dim mode with smooth brightness fades:
  - Default BRIGHTNESS=95 (USB charger).
  - When USB-CDC Serial is opened, target becomes USB_BRIGHTNESS_WHEN_HOST=15 (optional latch).
  - Fade timings: BRIGHTNESS_FADE_UP_MS / BRIGHTNESS_FADE_DOWN_MS.
- New artifact: tetris-main-serial-dim-v10-intro-dropfill-fade.zip

- Set BRIGHTNESS to 95 to match charger target (full brightness).

- v10c: Fix build error in intro (min() type mismatch) by replacing with uint32_t-safe ternary holdEnd computation.

- v10d: Fix linker error by adding missing MatrixDisplay::tickPowerBrightness() implementation (Serial-open dim + fade engine) to display_matrix_core.cpp.

2026-01-20
- v11: Intro is longer, speeds up over time (ramped frame delay + frames-per-piece), and ends with a 'bang' (white flashes + expanding ring) before clearing to game.

2026-01-20
- v12: Added big scrolling marquee title intro (default text "TETRIS" at scale 2) before dropfill intro; added BOOT_STATS_ENABLED (default false) to skip MAX level boot stats.

2026-01-20
- v12b: Fix build: remove duplicate config.h defines (fade macros, etc.) and repair main.cpp preprocessor gating (remove stray #endif) for BOOT_STATS_ENABLED.

2026-01-21
- v13: Made the in-game "level number drop-down" overlay optional via LEVEL_NUMBER_DROPDOWN_ENABLED (default false).

2026-01-21
- v14: Added a border-only "decade milestone" reveal animation when entering levels 11/21/31/... (new 10-level border style).
  - Short palette chase hugs the playfield border + quick corner wink; does not touch playfield pixels.
  - Config: MILESTONE_BORDER_REVEAL_ENABLED (default true), MILESTONE_BORDER_REVEAL_MS (default 1400).

2026-01-27
- Added serial debug preview keys for high score / end-of-run screens (b/o/p/t/m) plus MAX chase progress preview key (g).
- Fixed NEW MAX celebration number clipping for 10+ by auto-fitting digit scale in drawNumberCentered().
- Added persistent MAX-level chase attempts counter (Preferences key 'ma') and progress-bar style background on MAX screens.
- Updated MAX chase progress background to cycle through an effectively infinite set of colors:
  - Each time attempts reach MAX_LEVEL_CHASE_PROGRESS_STEPS, the background advances to a new hue.
  - Further attempts continue filling toward the next hue (no saturation to one color forever).

2026-01-26
- v16+: Added AI "smartness" ladder tied to MAX-level chase background cycles:
  - Each completed MAX chase fill cycle (full background color) increments AI decision quality.
  - Implemented as an AI skill level (0..AI_SMARTNESS_MAX) separate from AI speed profile.
  - Higher skill adds extra board features (row/col transitions, wells, landing-height) and at skill>=3 adds 1-ply lookahead using peekNextPieceType().
  - New config knobs: AI_SMARTNESS_FROM_MAX_CHASE_ENABLED / AI_SMARTNESS_BASE / AI_SMARTNESS_MAX.

2026-01-28
- Border glitch fix: boss-level (decade) locked-piece hue wipe no longer restarts mid-flight when pieces lock quickly; it only restarts after the previous 600ms wipe completes.
- Border glow scope: reactive "sphere" glow is now enabled only on decade levels (10/20/30/...), keeping non-decade levels classic.

2026-01-28
- AI incremental "learning": AI skill still steps up only when the MAX chase progress completes a full fill cycle (milestones unchanged),
  but now it also ramps within the cycle based on the per-attempt "color bar" fill:
  - main.cpp computes a 0..100 ramp percentage from attempts%STEPS.
  - ai.cpp blends heuristic weights toward the next tier and smoothly ramps lookahead strength (especially while approaching skill>=3).
